{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00292",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.24,
      "end_seconds": 5.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Doctor? Hi. I hope I've got the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.82,
      "end_seconds": 9.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "That's alright, take a seat. Tell me why you've come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.88,
      "end_seconds": 15.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Yeah, hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.14,
      "end_seconds": 20.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.86,
      "end_seconds": 26.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "I wanted to get shaky spells looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.55,
      "end_seconds": 29.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.43,
      "end_seconds": 38.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "It's been about three months, I'm fairly sure. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.13,
      "end_seconds": 46.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.19,
      "end_seconds": 58.85,
      "duration_seconds": 11.66,
      "text": "I'd give it a seven, out of ten. Eating something sweet helps a bit. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.85,
      "end_seconds": 62.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.51,
      "end_seconds": 69.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "A pounding heart with it goes along with it, you know, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.63,
      "end_seconds": 73.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "What's the pattern, is it there all day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.06,
      "end_seconds": 81.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "I'd say once or twice a day. I've also been feeling suddenly very hungry, since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.96,
      "end_seconds": 84.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Have you been sweating?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.05,
      "end_seconds": 93.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "Yeah. About a month, I'd say. Um, with sweating, it's severe, honestly. It's a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.6,
      "end_seconds": 98.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Right, is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.75,
      "end_seconds": 102.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.01,
      "end_seconds": 104.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Has there been any vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.01,
      "end_seconds": 109.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Okay, so not at all, no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 113.85,
      "end_seconds": 117.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice vomiting. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.01,
      "end_seconds": 123.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "So, uh, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.51,
      "end_seconds": 134.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.52,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any losing consciousness, seizure, chest pain or weight loss at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.56,
      "end_seconds": 139.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "No, um, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.03,
      "end_seconds": 141.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "And confusion, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.67,
      "end_seconds": 144.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "No, no confusion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.98,
      "end_seconds": 147.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.49,
      "end_seconds": 149.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.6,
      "end_seconds": 153.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.66,
      "end_seconds": 156.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.03,
      "end_seconds": 164.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.03,
      "end_seconds": 186.48,
      "duration_seconds": 19.45,
      "text": "Diabetes, for about ten years. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. High blood pressure, for nearly five years. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.72,
      "end_seconds": 188.69,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.07,
      "end_seconds": 198.78,
      "duration_seconds": 9.71,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known diabetes. We'll keep that in mind today. Yes, I can see the high blood pressure in your file as well. Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.47,
      "end_seconds": 210.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.8,
      "text": "Yes, I had my thyroid operated on, a long time ago. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.71,
      "end_seconds": 219.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "Okay, any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.67,
      "end_seconds": 223.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "I take glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 224.23,
      "end_seconds": 230.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the glimepiride was 4 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.04,
      "end_seconds": 235.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.94,
      "end_seconds": 241.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. Ramipril. I take it 5 milligrams, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.18,
      "end_seconds": 245.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.19,
      "end_seconds": 254.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "Sulfa drugs. I come out in... well, a rash. Uh, I'm allergic to codeine, I get feeling very drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.81,
      "end_seconds": 259.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.06,
      "end_seconds": 265.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "My mother has migraines. Um, my brother has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 266.75,
      "end_seconds": 279.03,
      "duration_seconds": 12.28,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 36.4 degrees, heart rate 86, weight 75 kilos. Height 163 centimetres, respiratory rate 18, pressure 108 over 73, BMI works out to 28.2, oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.97,
      "end_seconds": 280.85,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.92,
      "end_seconds": 286.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.38,
      "end_seconds": 289.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Stay still while I have a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.01,
      "end_seconds": 308.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Pulse is normal and there's no tremor right now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.54,
      "end_seconds": 322.27,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.54,
      "end_seconds": 327.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.13,
      "end_seconds": 328.83,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.98,
      "end_seconds": 351.59,
      "duration_seconds": 13.61,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with low sugar episodes related to diabetes medication. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I'd also keep a meal-timing issue in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.16,
      "end_seconds": 356.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "So, is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.26,
      "end_seconds": 373.6,
      "duration_seconds": 16.34,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like low sugar episodes related to diabetes medication, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had shaky spells for about three months, and no confusion or seizure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.09,
      "end_seconds": 377.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.57,
      "end_seconds": 380.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an HbA1c for diabetes control."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.65,
      "end_seconds": 383.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.29,
      "end_seconds": 409.68,
      "duration_seconds": 25.39,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a blood sugar test for hypoglycaemia. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Always keep glucose tablets or a sweet in your bag, and don't skip meals if you've taken your sugar tablet. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.46,
      "end_seconds": 417.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.26,
      "end_seconds": 421.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.15,
      "end_seconds": 429.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.55,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you black out or can't wake up properly after an episode."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 430.28,
      "end_seconds": 431.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.07,
      "end_seconds": 435.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Let's review you after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 436.92,
      "end_seconds": 438.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 440.38,
      "end_seconds": 443.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Okay, I think we're finished. Is everything clear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 444.4,
      "end_seconds": 448.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Yeah, no, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 451.68,
      "end_seconds": 452.4,
      "duration_seconds": 0.72,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}